SteamARM: a game covering a display hides the Dock and the menu bar

In "fullscreen windowed" a game's layer covers the whole display, but the
Dock and the menu bar stayed over it ("el dock siempre se ve por encima",
the user, Counter-Strike 2): not fullscreen at all on a Mac. The hiding
(XQUARTZ_RL_PRESENTATION) is now on by default, while the X server is the
active application; another application brings them back, as for every
fullscreen program. A layer that leaves for a moment (a swapchain made
again) is given 400 ms before the Dock returns. The blinking measured with
the 100 ms overlay watch on as well stays avoided: the watch is off.
XQUARTZ_RL_PRESENTATION=0 restores the old behaviour.
